					<h3 class="project-title text-xl md:text-2xl font-bold" id="p-sycaudit-title">SycAudit</h3>
					<p class="project-desc text-slate-300 text-base leading-relaxed">
						A research project auditing and evaluating sycophancy in AI systems. Responses are
						generated across an N×M grid of prompt framings, annotated under a frozen five-facet
						rubric — excessive agreement, flattery, avoidance of disagreement, preference alignment
						and unnecessary validation — and scored by an in-house ML grader (MLP and XGBoost over
						BGE/GTE sentence embeddings) trained on a leakage-checked annotated corpus with frozen
						splits. A full-stack application (FastAPI + React + PostgreSQL) computes a per-response
						WOBBLE score and surfaces the least-sycophantic answer alongside its facet breakdown.
					</p>
