					<h3 class="project-title text-xl md:text-2xl font-bold" id="p-vriddhi-title">VRIDDHI</h3>
					<p class="project-desc text-slate-300 text-base leading-relaxed">
						An AI-driven hyper-local business advisory and financial structuring system for rural
						micro-entrepreneurs. The architecture keeps a hard boundary: market intelligence,
						reach estimation and opportunity scoring are <strong>deterministic, code-driven stages</strong> —
						the LLM is not the market-analysis engine. Only after the evidence package is assembled
						does a single LLM call produce plain-language advisory, which a hermetic validation layer
						checks against that evidence (invented values, contradictions, coverage) before anything
						is displayed. A parallel RAG pipeline answers government-scheme questions with retrieval-grounded,
						validated responses, backed by deterministic financial and risk engines.
					</p>
